title: The JWKS answer must be checked before it is cached
updated: 2026-10-20T09:23:37Z
---

The JWKS answer is cached without a check.

lib/WWW/Authentik/OIDC.pm:205 puts ->{data} into the cache without looking at it.

Failure case: the JWKS endpoint answers 200 with HTML. _jwks stays undef, and verify_token (OIDC.pm:252-260) throws away a valid token with "kid_keys lookup failed", because decode_jwt fails on undef.

Decide: before the caching is checked that the answer is a hash with keys, otherwise an API error is raised.

Implemented on branch k4-k7, commit 34a651d.

WWW::Authentik::OIDC::jwks checks the answer before it is cached: an answer
that is no hash with a keys array throws WWW::Authentik::Error::API naming
the method, the URL and the status, and nothing is cached.

verify_token fetches the keys out of the try block, so such an answer is an
error of its own and not a token that is rejected.

Test: t/62-oidc-jwks.t (new). It was red against the old lib as failed
expectations: jwks answered without an error, verify_token rejected the
token with 'kid_keys lookup failed'.

Offline suite: prove -lr t, Files=12 Tests=71, all green.

Also found: the async twin Net::Async::Authentik::OIDC needs the same check
and the same change in verify_token; it is not touched from this repo.

Erledigt in 34a651d, nach main gezogen. Der JWKS-Endpunkt wird geprueft: eine Antwort ohne keys-Array ist ein API-Fehler mit Methode, URL und Status, und es wird nichts gecacht. verify_token holt die Schluessel ausserhalb des try-Blocks, damit eine kaputte JWKS-Antwort ein Fehler der Instanz ist und nicht ein abgelehntes Token. Rot-Nachweis: t/62-oidc-jwks.t ist gegen das alte lib/ rot (7 fehlgeschlagene Erwartungen in 2 Subtests, kein die).
